# Python Style

This rule file describes style conventions for Python code.

## String Formatting

- Prefer `.format()` over f-strings or `%` formatting.
  - Example: `"Invalid type '{}'. Must be one of: {}".format(type_input, ', '.join(VALID_TYPES))`
  - Example: `"{}.{}.md".format(i, news_type)` instead of `f"{i}.{news_type}.md"`
- When formatting with multiple parameters, put each parameter on its own line for readability.
  - Example:
    ```python
    "Invalid type '{}'. Must be one of: {}".format(
        type_input,
        ', '.join(VALID_TYPES)
    )
    ```
